.TH AWS-LC-OPENSSL 1 "November 2026" "aws-lc 5.13.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aws-lc-openssl \- OpenSSL-compatible command line tool built on AWS-LC
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aws-lc-openssl
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aws-lc-openssl
is AWS-LC's implementation of a subset of the
.BR openssl (1)
command line tool. It is installed under this name so that it does not
replace the OpenSSL tool. Run it without arguments, or with
.BR help ,
to list the commands.
.PP
Commands: asn1parse, ca, crl, dgst, dhparam, ec, ecparam, enc, genpkey,
genrsa, md5, ocsp, pkcs12, pkcs8, pkey, pkeyutl, rand, rehash, req, rsa,
sha1, s_client, verify, version, x509. Options follow the OpenSSL tool where
a command is implemented; not every OpenSSL option is supported.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openssl (1),
.BR aws-lc-bssl (1),
.BR aws-lc-c_rehash (1)
